=== 7. R7g asset content binding (PARTIAL by design) ==========================
Producer: new shared helper v11-spec-common.cjs assetDigestsOf(exampleDir, spec.assets)
  -> each evidence row now carries assetDigests:[{path,bytes,hash,present}].
  Wired into all three result records (v11-examples-verify ui + app paths,
  v11-devtools-examples). Consumer: S15 block now checks existence, non-zero size,
  then byte-for-byte agreement with the evidence record.
  Contract choice: digests live in EVIDENCE, not in example.json, because adding a
  spec field would change every specFingerprint and mass-invalidate otherwise
  valid evidence. Still OPEN: the digest is taken from the same working tree as the
  run, so it detects post-capture replacement/garbage but cannot prove provenance
  of an asset that was already wrong at capture time (that needs upstream
  provenance, cf. R1 license work). Reported as PARTIAL, not closed.
  Controls (gltf-basic/assets/BoxTextured.glb, 5956 B, captured hash b510eca2e2ef33f6):
    NC-D1 truncate to 0 bytes -> "S15-FREEZE: §15：assets/BoxTextured.glb 为 0 字节"  EXIT 1  DETECTED
    NC-D2 same-size garbage   -> "S15-ASSET-BIND: 内容哈希 fc722a727f2a06ff ≠ 证据 hash=b510eca2e2ef33f6（资产内容被替换）"  EXIT 1  DETECTED
    RESTORE -> both clears (gltf-basic fully clean, 10 fails remain = other examples'
              pre-binding evidence at that moment)
  (F-39 previously: 0-byte and garbage assets both left the offline gate GREEN.)

